# Keema Matar

Based on [https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/keema-matar](https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/keema-matar) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251124112532/https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/keema-matar))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Spice Base

- [ ] 15 g [Cooking oil]{ ing="cooking-oil" } (a drizzle)
- [ ] 5 g [Mustard seeds]{ ing="mustard-seeds" } (a spoonful, whole or ground)
- [ ] 5 g [Cumin]{ ing="cumin" } (a spoonful, whole or ground)
- [ ] 3 g [Black peppercorns]{ ing="black-peppercorns" } (1/2 spoonful, whole or ground)
- [ ] 2-3 [Whole cloves]{ ing="whole-cloves" }
- [ ] 1 [Bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" }
- [ ] 1/2 stick [Ground cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" } (whole)
- [ ] 5 g [Turmeric powder]{ ing="turmeric-powder" } (a spoonful)
- [ ] 5 g [Chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" } (a spoonful)
- [ ] 2 g [Garam masala]{ ing="garam-masala" } (a sprinkle)

### Aromatics

- [ ] 1/2 [Onion]{ ing="onion" }, diced
- [ ] 2 cloves [Garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, grated or minced
- [ ] 1[” knob Fresh ginger]{ ing="knob-fresh-ginger" }, grated or minced
- [ ] 2-3 [Green chilies]{ ing="green-chilies" }, minced
- [ ] 2-3 [Roma tomatoes]{ ing="roma-tomatoes" }, grated
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" }, a sprinkle

### Beef Base

- [ ] 450 g [Ground beef]{ ing="ground-beef" }
- [ ] 200 g [Water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" }, a sprinkle
- [ ] 200 g [Frozen peas]{ ing="frozen-peas" }
- [ ] [Lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, a squeeze
- [ ] [Garam masala]{ ing="garam-masala" }, a sprinkle

### For Serving

- [ ] [Basmati rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" }, cooked
- [ ] [Cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, roughly chopped (for garnish)
- [ ] [Roti flatbreads]{ ing="roti-flatbreads" } (optional)

## Recipe

1. Prep the spices and beef base by crushing [mustard seeds]{ ing="mustard-seeds" }, [cumin]{ ing="cumin" } seeds, and [peppercorns]{ ing="black-peppercorns" } in a mortar and pestle if whole. Leave [cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" } stick, [cloves]{ ing="whole-cloves" }, and [bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" } whole for removal later. Grate [tomatoes]{ ing="roma-tomatoes" } and set aside. Soften [ground beef]{ ing="ground-beef" } by mixing with 50% [water]{ ing="water" } in a bowl until smooth and clump-free.
1. Toast the spices and aromatics by heating [oil]{ ing="cooking-oil" } in a pan over medium heat. Add cinnamon stick, cloves, bay leaf, ground peppercorns, mustard seed, and cumin; bloom for 10-20 seconds until fragrant. Add remaining aromatics (except tomato) and sauté 1-2 minutes until softened.
1. Add tomato and remaining spices by stirring in [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }, turmeric, [garam masala]{ ing="garam-masala" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" }; cook 30 seconds. Add grated tomatoes and reduce for 5 minutes. Deglaze with water if dry.
1. Add the beef by turning heat to high. Add ground meat mixture with salt; break apart while simmering 8-10 minutes until cooked through and thickened.
1. Add [peas]{ ing="frozen-peas" } and finish by lowering heat to low. Toss in peas and stir until cooked through. Turn off heat. Add [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" } and final garam masala sprinkle. Taste and adjust seasonings as needed.
1. Serve with [rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" } or [flatbreads]{ ing="roti-flatbreads" }; garnish with fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }.

## Notes

- Serves 2-4 in 1 hour
- Keema matar roughly translates to “minced meat & peas”
- An easy and delicious upgrade to all the other ground meat recipes
